{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "title": "Why Does MPC Converge? A One-Step Proof",
  "summary": "Model predictive control plans a whole path, takes one step and plans again. Why should that ever reach the target? This episode follows one number, the remaining action: the bill still left to pay. The old plan, shifted by one step and capped with a reference step, shows that the bill falls by at least each step's cost, for every window length, once one test on one step passes; a worked example checks it with numbers.",
